        "title": "Simplify GitHub comment actions",
        "body": "Make ordinary comment actions straightforward.\n\nConceptually:\n\n```text\ncomment_issue / comment_pr\n  \u2192 resolve body\n  \u2192 post one ordinary GitHub comment\n  \u2192 return the GitHub result\n```\n\nRemove hidden GitWeave markers, hashing, full comment-history scans, and retry reconciliation unless a concrete duplicate-comment problem is observed later.\n\nKeep only validation and behavior directly required to post the requested comment and report failures.\n\nThis change implements the behavior above with focused regression coverage and documentation.\n\nValidation: deterministic regression tests and independent GitWeave review; GitHub CI on the published changes.\n\nCloses #34."
